@*
    A step's state as a dot at the head of its row: the compact form of a FlowSteps
    node, for a list that already says the state in a word beside it. The Sessions
    pane's stage rows are the case — a dot, the stage, and "Failed" or "Not yet" or
    the time it took further along the row.

    Decorative, and only ever drawn beside the word: the dot is aria-hidden, so a
    screen reader hears the word once rather than a colour it cannot see
    (.devbook/design/accessibility.md). The five tones are FlowSteps', told apart by
    shape as well as colour — done filled, active filled inside a ring, blocked a
    filled square, pending and skipped hollow rings, skipped's dashed.
*@
<span class="@ClassValue" aria-hidden="true" data-tone="@Slug" data-testid="@TestId"></span>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public FlowStepTone Tone { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; }

    private string Slug => Tone.ToString().ToLowerInvariant();

    private string ClassValue =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CssClass) ? $"status-dot status-dot--{Slug}" : $"status-dot status-dot--{Slug} {CssClass}";
}
